# ghcr.io/liken-sh/indi-qhy: QHY cameras. The QHY focuser needs no SDK,
# so it is in indi-open.
sdk libqhyccd
driver indi_qhy_ccd
# Many QHY cameras power up as a bare Cypress EZ-USB chip, and the host
# writes the camera's firmware into the chip before the driver can open
# it. On a Linux distribution, a udev rule of libqhy runs fxload when the
# bare chip appears. A liken machine runs no udev, so firmware-operator
# runs fxload from this image in a pod instead, and
# observatory-operator's deploy/firmware/ holds one Firmware object for
# each rule. Ubuntu installs fxload at /sbin/fxload, where /sbin is a
# link to usr/sbin. The image keeps that link, so the program's path in
# the package's file list holds in the image and its copyright file
# travels with it, and puts fxload on PATH, which names only /usr/bin.
seed /usr/sbin/fxload
link /sbin usr/sbin
link /usr/bin/fxload ../sbin/fxload
# The firmware files that the rules name, and the rules file itself, which
# observatory-operator's make firmware-rules reads from this image.
data /usr/lib/firmware/qhy
data /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/85-qhyccd.rules
# The libqhy directory of indi-3rdparty holds no license file. The
# copyright file of its own Debian package, debian/libqhy/copyright,
# names QHY CCD as the copyright holder, so it travels with the SDK and
# the firmware.
license debian/libqhy/copyright
